# WN22-AC-000050: Windows Server 2022 maximum password age must be configured to 60 days or less.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-ac-000050-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 maximum password age must be configured to 60 days or less.`
    description `The longer a password is in use, the greater the opportunity for someone to gain unauthorized knowledge of the passwords. Scheduled changing of passwords hinders the ability of unauthorized system users to crack passwords and gain access to a system.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,account-policy,security-policy`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-53:IA-5(1)(H)`
    control_objective `WN22-AC-000050`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Password Policy >> Maximum password age to "60" days or less (excluding "0", which is unacceptable).`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_IA_5_1_H `Windows Server implements IA-5(1)(H) by enforcing MaximumPasswordAge per the STIG (Maximum password age must be 1-60 days (nonzero and <= 60).). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `MaximumPasswordAge`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int >= 1
        value_int int <= 60
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
